+# Epic 4 Context: Crisis Model
+
+<!-- Compiled from planning artifacts. Edit freely. Regenerate with compile-epic-context if planning docs change. -->
+
+## Goal
+
+Deliver fair, predictable crises: the player reads warning signs (node 🟡/🔴, pipe pressure,
+demand forecast) with lead times, predicts the Surge, and survives it — "I should have seen
+this coming," never random `[FORGE #3]`. MVP ships the Surge archetype (forecast 10× demand
+spike that cascades into saturation if unprepared). The epic is the fairness contract of the
+whole game: every crisis is the consequence of a topology flaw the player could have
+prevented, foreshadowed by readable warnings, with a structured root cause + a preventive
+redesign.
+
+## Stories
+
+- Story 4.1: Warning signs + forecast (strain metrics → 🟡/🔴 + pipe pressure + demand
+  forecast with lead times; the forecast "weather report" panel).
+- Story 4.2: Surge SetPiece + Crisis Engine (root-cause, fair).
+- Story 4.3: Network Health meter + win/lose/retry.
+- (E3.3/E3.4 health states + readability feed 4.1's warning surface; E4.4 remaining
+  archetypes are E10.)
+
+## Requirements & Constraints
+
+- **Warning-first fairness:** every crisis is foreshadowed by readable warning signs with a
+  lead time ≥ the player's reaction window; no crisis on a healthy within-capacity topology.
+  Lead times (GDD Numerical Design): node strained ~30 s, node critical ~10 s, pipe pressure
+  ~20 s, demand forecast 15–60 s.
+- **Traceable strain:** a 🔴 node is always traceable to a measured strain; health
+  transitions fire on defined thresholds (strain ≥ 70 % strained, ≥ 90 % critical —
+  art-direction §6.1; thresholds live in `balance.json`).
+- **Color is never the sole encoder:** every warning state pairs color with icon + shape +
+  outline (triple-redundant — colorblind-safe, reduced-motion-safe; the ring pulse rate is
+  itself the escalation signal: slow ~1.2 Hz strained, fast ~2.5 Hz critical).
+- **Forecast reads, never fires:** the forecast "weather report" names incoming SetPieces
+  with a countdown; it READS the schedule (set-piece `forecast_lead_ticks`), it does not
+  trigger anything (that is the Crisis Engine, story 4.2).
+- **Root-cause fairness (test contracts):** no crisis without a warning + lead time; every
+  crisis has ≥ 1 topology redesign that would have prevented it; recovery always possible.
+
+## Technical Decisions
+
+- **S4 Crisis Engine** evaluates **downstream of flow** each tick: reads Topology + Flow
+  state, emits `Warning_Raised` / `Crisis_Triggered` / `Crisis_Resolved` events (ODN-14). It
+  never owns the demand timeline — the Director (ODN-7) is upstream and gets a read-only
+  view; a crisis is a consequence, never its own cause (structural, `[REVIEW M1]`).
+- **Data-driven archetypes:** the archetype table lives in `crises.json`
+  (`archetype, root_cause_pattern, warning_curve, lead_time_ticks, failure_effect`); the
+  Surge is content + evaluation procs, not re-architecture (ODN-4). SetPieces already carry
+  `forecast_lead_ticks` in `demand.json` and the demand director already multiplies their
+  class's spawn volume while active.
+- **Run_State owns `Crisis_State (warnings[], active[], forecast[])`** (§8.2) alongside
+  Topology/Flow/Health; all sim state integer-only, no maps, no file/clock reads (ODN-1/10).
+- **Golden discipline:** warning/forecast state rides the T1 hash (replay-equality E10) via
+  append-only serialization (absent-when-empty sections; new event tags append); T2 pixel
+  goldens of the forecast + warning state; deliberate re-blesses carry proof.
+- Strain metrics come from Topology + Flow each tick (utilization vs throughput; node
+  throughput from `node_types.json`; bundle capacity from the static bundle view).
+
+## UX & Interaction Patterns
+
+- Node health is the primary warning surface: a node glows its state color with a ring
+  outline + an icon (check / `!` / `!!`), ring pulses at the state's rate — never color
+  alone.
+- The forecast "weather report" panel is the P3 fairness surface: names the incoming
+  SetPiece with a countdown, so the player sees the surge coming and has time to redesign.
+- Alert tiles use `⚠️ <BRAND>: <STATE>` format — color + glyph + caption, never color alone.
+
+## Cross-Story Dependencies
+
+- 4.1 (warnings + forecast + strain telegraph) precedes 4.2 (Surge firing + root cause) and
+  4.3 (Network Health win/lose) — 4.1 only ever *names* trouble; firing lands in 4.2.
+- 4.1 consumes the 3.1 demand director (SetPiece schedule + `forecast_lead_ticks`), 3.2/3.3
+  QoS + contention (the strain the flow produces), 3.4 SLA accumulators (the same event seam
+  feeds the health layer).
+- E3.3/E3.4 (health states + readability) are design content of the same warning surface;
+  story 5.2 later re-drives them from the growing map.
