+# warn.dem — Story 4.1's launchable golden: the forecast + strain telegraph.
+# Era 3 (the streaming-surge era): the director spawns email 4/tick res->res
+# + streaming 2/tick host->res. Pipe 1-2 (router->host) is DELAYED to 30s, so
+# the streaming packets pile at the HOST (no route — the routing table gives
+# complete paths only): the honest node telegraph. Golden-verified stream:
+#   host Node_Strained @1 (2 waiting = 75% of the 80 u/s host throughput),
+#   host Node_Critical @2 (4 waiting = 150%), red until the 30s draw opens
+#   the route (the pre-draw email spawns briefly redden the residentials too
+#   — no routes exist before the 100ms draws apply at tick 3; they clear the
+#   same tick). The forecast panel appears at 30s (the surge's 600-tick lead)
+#   and counts down (verified: countdown 300 @45s); the surge fires at 60s
+#   (streaming x10 — the director's demand multiplier) and the panel reads
+#   NOW. Pipe 0 (res0->router) saturates under the email load -> the pressure
+#   halo runs red/amber (a lane at its E9 bound = dropping). Captures:
+#   1500ms = the strain telegraph before the forecast; 45000ms = panel
+#   countdown + red pressure; 65000ms = surge ACTIVE (NOW). The T1 pins the
+#   forecast rows + the whole warning event stream (E10).
+seed 4243
+run 75000ms
+era 3
+fixture qos
+expect hash stable
+at 100ms draw 0 1 standard
+at 100ms draw 3 1 standard
+at 100ms draw 4 1 standard
+at 30000ms draw 1 2 standard
+capture at 1500ms
+capture at 45000ms
+capture at 65000ms
